3OO NORTH STREETWEST LAFAYETTE, INDIAN A47905755-775-5L75Ensuring West Lofoyette is olwoys o safe ond greot ploce to work, live, ond play.
January Training Report
This month, we had Lieutenant Ben Jones attend the NationaI Fire Academy.Lieutenant Jones compteted the Command and Control of lncident 0perations course. Wehave had several of our officers complete this week-tong course.January's monthly medica[ training inctuded atl our members being recertified in CPR.This is a two-year certification through the American Heart Association.Fire training for January was conducted jointty with the Lafayette Fire Department atHarner Lake. 0ur crews performed an ice rescue scenario, working atongside members ofthe Lafayette Fire Department. Tippecanoe Emergency Management Agency members werethere to assist with the training.0ur members were assigned numerous online training to be compteted throughoutthe year. This covers the 30 hours of mandatory training required by OHSA. Each member isrequired to complete 228 hours of training each year.TotaI person-hours spent training in January was 1154.5 hours.
Reported byCaptain Birge

