WESTLAFAYETTE
REPORT
FIRE DEPARTMENT
Ensuring West Lafayette is always a safe and great place to work, live, and play.
TO: West Lafayette Common CouncilFROM: Jeff A. Need, Fire ChiefDATE: February 5,2024SUBJECT: January 2024 Fire Report
Call Totals: West Lafayette Fire responded to 315 Total Calls in January: 208 Medica|4Fire, 9 Hazardous Condition, 34 Service Calls, 44 False Alarms, 2 Special lncidents, and 14Other.
Traininq: January's monthly fire training included joint training with the Lafayette FireDepartment, performing ice rescue scenarios at Harner Lake. TEMA (Tippecanoe EmergencyManagement Agency) members were also on hand. t\Iedical training consisted of mandatorydepartment-wide CPR recertification with the American Heart Association. Lieutenant BenJones completed the Command and Control of lncident Operations course at the National FireAcademy. lt/embers performed numerous online training assignments as part of their yearlymandatory OSHA training. This brought the total training hours in January to 1154.5.
lnspections: The lnspection Division's January fire prevention and education included 111general inspections, S re-inspections, 17 newconstruction inspections, 15 plan reviews, 1consultation, 65 documentation reports and reviews, 36 code reviews, 1 fire alarm test, 5sprinkler system tests, and 10 fire drills, bringing the January overall total to 273.
Respectfully subm itted,
Mft4,,L
Jeff A. NeedFire Chief, City of West Lafayette
300 North Street I West Lafayette, lN 47906 | (765)775-5175 | westlafayette.in.qov/fire

endstream 
